# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and never committed.
#
# These are consumed at CMAKE-CONFIGURE time, not at build time and not at
# runtime: CMakeLists.txt declares them as cache variables and
# compiles them into the image as PICO_TIME_WIFI_SSID / PICO_TIME_WIFI_PASSWORD
# string definitions. Two consequences follow, and both need checking:
#
#   1. dev.py does NOT source this file. Pass the values through explicitly:
#
#        BUILD_ARGS="-DPICO_TIME_WIFI_SSID=$WIFI_SSID
#        -DPICO_TIME_WIFI_PASSWORD=$WIFI_PASSWORD
#        -DPICO_LWIPOPTS_TARGET=pico_time_lwipopts_fallback" \
#          python3 dev.py build --tree firmware
#
#   2. The values are baked into an existing build tree's cache. Changing them
#      needs a reconfigure; a stale cache silently produces firmware that
#      cannot join, which for this library means NTP never resolves and the
#      wall clock never leaves its epoch. Verify before flashing:
#
#        strings build-firmware/examples/ntp_sync/pico_time_ntp_sync.elf \
#          | grep -c "$WIFI_SSID"
#
# The two names below are the shell variables this file defines; the cmake
# cache variables they feed are namespaced PICO_TIME_WIFI_*, like every other
# knob in the family. This file is the developer's, not a repository's, so
# one .env serves every repo on the machine.
#
# WPA2-PSK only. The CYW43439 on the Pico 2 W does not do WPA3 or enterprise.

WIFI_SSID=
WIFI_PASSWORD=
